00:01:38.090 --> 00:01:41.660
Why don't we start with the
fact that Cloud IoT Core is now

00:01:41.660 --> 00:01:42.719
generally available.

00:01:42.719 --> 00:01:44.510
If you're not familiar
with Cloud IoT Core,

00:01:44.510 --> 00:01:46.970
it is our fully-managed
service to help securely

00:01:46.970 --> 00:01:50.129
connect and manage your
IoT devices at scale.

00:01:50.129 --> 00:01:51.170
That's all the buzzwords.

00:01:51.170 --> 00:01:51.650
MELANIE WARRICK: Yes.

00:01:51.650 --> 00:01:52.691
That's all the buzzwords.

00:01:52.691 --> 00:01:54.285
And apparently,
this general release

00:01:54.285 --> 00:01:56.360
is incorporating a
few new features.

00:01:56.360 --> 00:01:59.510
You can now publish data streams
from the IoT Core protocol

00:01:59.510 --> 00:02:01.400
bridge to multiple
Cloud Pub/Sub topics,

00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:03.200
and you can simplify
deployments.

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:03.960
So, check it out.

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:04.710
MARK MANDEL: Yeah.

00:02:04.710 --> 00:02:06.740
And we have a whole bunch of
device partners and application

00:02:06.740 --> 00:02:07.650
partners, as well.

00:02:07.650 --> 00:02:09.770
So if there are particular
devices or application

00:02:09.770 --> 00:02:12.228
platforms that you need to be
able to use, check those out.

00:02:12.228 --> 00:02:14.040
We'll have a list
there in the blog post.

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:16.165
MELANIE WARRICK: Another
thing we have for the week

00:02:16.165 --> 00:02:18.800
is that JupyterLab is
apparently ready in beta

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:20.990
and accessible for all users.

00:02:20.990 --> 00:02:23.030
And JupyterLab is
actually coming out

00:02:23.030 --> 00:02:24.440
of the Jupyter Group.

00:02:24.440 --> 00:02:27.680
And Jupyter is based originally
off of this notebook that's

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:31.190
become very popular in the data
science space, in particular.

00:02:31.190 --> 00:02:33.462
This notebook allows
users to create and share

00:02:33.462 --> 00:02:35.420
documents that combine
live code with narrative

00:02:35.420 --> 00:02:37.910
text, mathematical
equations, visualizations,

00:02:37.910 --> 00:02:41.000
interactive controls,
and other output sources.

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:42.890
It's really a useful tool.

00:02:42.890 --> 00:02:44.879
And so they built JupyterLab.

00:02:44.879 --> 00:02:46.670
And JupyterLab, in
particular, is something

00:02:46.670 --> 00:02:48.710
that they're using as this
interactive development

00:02:48.710 --> 00:02:50.335
environment for
working with notebooks.

00:02:50.335 --> 00:02:54.320
So it is able to integrate
with text editors, terminals,

00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:57.410
data file viewers, and
other custom components,

00:02:57.410 --> 00:03:01.400
and allow you to basically do
a more comprehensive workflow.

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:02.030
Check it out.

00:03:02.030 --> 00:03:02.720
It's really interesting.

00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:04.160
And we're going to
actually have a link where

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:05.576
you can find out
more information

00:03:05.576 --> 00:03:06.950
and figure out
how to install it.

00:03:06.950 --> 00:03:07.825
MARK MANDEL: Awesome.

00:03:07.825 --> 00:03:10.730
For another one, we announced
that Google Cloud Spanner

00:03:10.730 --> 00:03:13.220
can now be used as a
vault storage backend.

00:03:13.220 --> 00:03:15.260
If you're not familiar
with HashiCorp Vault,

00:03:15.260 --> 00:03:16.820
it's a really cool
open source tool

00:03:16.820 --> 00:03:18.112
for basically managing secrets.

00:03:18.112 --> 00:03:20.486
It's very popular, of course,
with Google Cloud Platform,

00:03:20.486 --> 00:03:21.800
as well as Kubernetes.

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:24.740
This is kind of cool because
Spanner is a great way

00:03:24.740 --> 00:03:27.800
to have high availability
across multiple regions

00:03:27.800 --> 00:03:29.116
and have that as a back end.

00:03:29.116 --> 00:03:31.490
So it enables a few things on
Vault that are kind of neat

00:03:31.490 --> 00:03:33.680
in terms of like
transactional support as well,

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:35.930
enterprise grade security--
it basically uses the same

00:03:35.930 --> 00:03:38.340
security as Cloud Spanner,
which is amazing--

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:40.790
and it's also supported by
Google, which is also nice.

00:03:40.790 --> 00:03:41.660
MELANIE WARRICK: If you
want to get started,

00:03:41.660 --> 00:03:43.190
you should download
and install the latest

00:03:43.190 --> 00:03:44.490
version of HashiCorp Vault.

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:48.200
MARK MANDEL: 0.9.4,
apparently, at time of reading.

00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:49.550
MELANIE WARRICK: Good to know.

00:03:49.550 --> 00:03:52.009
